<title>NEW ZEALAND: Summary of RBNZ economic projections.</title>
<headline>Summary of RBNZ economic projections.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a summary of key economic projections released by the Reserve Bank of New Zealand on Thursday.</p>
<p>Figures in brackets are forecasts released by the RB in their September forecasts, except inflation series which are from the December Monetary Policy Statement.</p>
<p>Figures are for March years (except budget balance which in June):</p>
<p>					1997	  1998	  1999</p>
<p>GDP (pct)			   2.0 (2.0)   2.7 (2.4)   3.9</p>
<p>Budget surplus (pct of GDP)   2.0 (3.8)   1.9 (2.4)   1.6</p>
<p>Current account dfct ($bln)   5.5 (3.6)   5.4 (4.0)   6.2</p>
<p>CPI inflation (pct)	     2.2 (2.1)   1.1 (0.5)   1.0 (0.1)</p>
<p>Underlying inflation (pct)    2.2 (2.0)   1.2 (0.5)   1.1 (0.2)</p>
<p>Unemployment (pct)		6.3 (6.6)   6.3 (7.0)   5.5</p>
<p>Employment growth (pct)	 1.6 (1.2)   1.4 (0.4)   2.6</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
